{"stem": "observe_float", "name": "observe_float", "description": "Observe Float \u2014 emit an event when a float parameter changes.\n\nCompares the `value` parameter to its value in the previous audio block.\nWhen the value differs, fires a float event carrying the new value.\n\nThe detection uses a per-sample state loop whose state variable holds the\nprevious block's parameter value.  At sample 0 of each block the state\nequals last block's value; from sample 1 onward both sides equal the\ncurrent value, so only one change can fire per block.\n\nParameters:\n  value   \u2014 float to observe (full practical range)\n\nEvents:\n  changed (event_float) \u2014 fires at sample 0 of any block where value\n                          differs from the previous block's value;\n                          carries the new value", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-03 23:12 UTC", "git_commit": "4f41407", "compiled_with": "f435c63"}, "wasm": "observe_float.wasm", "meta_file": "observe_float.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "value", "type": "float", "min": -1e+20, "max": 1e+20, "default": 0.0, "float_index": 0}], "samplers": [], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [], "meters": [{"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}], "event_outputs": [{"name": "changed", "type": "float", "fired_index": 0, "value_index": 0, "subtype": "param_changed"}], "has_visualizer": true, "has_audio_output": false, "viz_width": 512, "viz_height": 256, "compiled_with": "f435c63"}, "mca": {"graph": "observe_float", "block_size": 512, "results": [{"label": "Intel Haswell (x86-64-v3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "haswell", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 1.4204, "block_rthroughput": 83.25, "cycles_per_sample": 0.1626, "insns_per_block": 219, "uops_per_block": 333}, {"label": "Intel Skylake-AVX512 (x86-64-v4)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86